    "title": "The Ache Above the Fifth",
    "summary": "Aeolian's only avoid note is the b6 sitting a half step above the 5; Dorian removes it by raising that degree a whole tone, and each of the two mode families turns out to hold exactly one mode — the one with the raised dial — that has no avoid note at all.",
