    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The definition already exists: an avoid note is a scale tone sitting a half step above a chord tone — a note to move through, not one to land on and hold. "
        },
        {
          "text": "The Note That Fights the Chord",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "modes-the-avoid-note"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " is where that got worked out in full; this lesson puts it to work on a minor tonic."
        }
      ]
    },
