    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The Note That Fights the Chord",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "modes-the-avoid-note"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " called Lydian the only one of its three modes without an avoid note, and scoped that claim on purpose — because Dorian has none either. Across the six modes of the two families, each family holds exactly one mode with no avoid note over its own tonic triad — and in both cases it's the mode with the raised dial: Lydian raises the "
        },
        {
          "text": "4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", Dorian raises the "
        },
        {
          "text": "6",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". That is a fact about these six, and about the seventh it says nothing at all."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Phrygian has two — one above the root, one above the fifth — the only one of the six that does. Why that matters is Phrygian's own business, and it comes later."
        }
      ]
    },
